tasks.model:
def format_book(book: dict) -> str:
    """One line for a book: title, author and year."""
    return f"{book['title']} by {book['author']} ({book['year']})"

tasks.prompt:
Build the whole tool. Keep the **books** list as given and write:

- **format_book(book)** as before;
- **search(books, text, field="title")**: the books whose field contains text, ignoring capitals;
- **report(books, text, field="title")**: the found books oldest first; print **N found for "text" in field**, then **- ** and a formatted line for each.

Then ask **Search for? ** and **In title or author? ** (blank means title, and ignore capitals) and call report.
